<section id="faq" class="section" style="padding:120px 0; position:relative;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head center" style="margin-bottom:60px; max-width:760px; margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto; text-align:center;">
      <span class="section-label">
        <span style="display:block; width:28px; height:1px; background:var(--ink);"></span>
        07 · FAQ
      </span>
      <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size:clamp(34px, 5vw, 64px); font-weight:700; line-height:1.02; letter-spacing:-0.04em; margin-bottom:18px;">
        Common questions.<br><span class="serif" style="font-family:var(--serif); font-weight:400; letter-spacing:-0.02em; font-style:italic;">Straight</span> answers.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list reveal" style="display:grid; gap:12px; max-width:820px; margin:0 auto;">
      <details class="faq-item" style="background:var(--bg-card); border:var(--ink-line); box-shadow:var(--ink-stamp); border-radius:var(--radius); overflow:hidden; transition:all 0.25s ease;">
        <summary class="faq-q" style="width:100%; border:none; background:transparent; padding:22px 26px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; font-family:var(--sans); font-size:17px; font-weight:600; color:var(--ink); text-align:left; letter-spacing:-0.015em; cursor:pointer; list-style:none;">
          What is AgentCall?
          <span class="sign" style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:50%; border:var(--ink-thin); background:var(--bg-card); box-shadow:2px 2px 0 var(--ink); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; transition:all 0.25s ease; flex-shrink:0;">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M 4.5 12 C 8 11.8, 14 12.2, 19.5 12"/><path d="M 12 4.5 C 11.8 8, 12.2 14, 12 19.5"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-a" style="max-height:0; overflow:hidden; transition:max-height 0.4s ease;">
          <div class="faq-a-inner" style="padding:0 26px 22px 26px; color:var(--muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">
            AgentCall is a skill for AI agents — it lets any agent (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Gemini, Windsurf, Junie, OpenClaw, and more) join video meetings on Google Meet, Zoom, and Microsoft Teams. The agent listens, speaks at the right moments, shares screens, and collaborates — just like a real teammate.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:var(--bg-card); border:var(--ink-line); box-shadow:var(--ink-stamp); border-radius:var(--radius); overflow:hidden; transition:all 0.25s ease;">
        <summary class="faq-q" style="width:100%; border:none; background:transparent; padding:22px 26px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; font-family:var(--sans); font-size:17px; font-weight:600; color:var(--ink); text-align:left; letter-spacing:-0.015em; cursor:pointer; list-style:none;">
          Which meeting platforms are supported?
          <span class="sign" style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:50%; border:var(--ink-thin); background:var(--bg-card); box-shadow:2px 2px 0 var(--ink); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; transition:all 0.25s ease; flex-shrink:0;">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M 4.5 12 C 8 11.8, 14 12.2, 19.5 12"/><path d="M 12 4.5 C 11.8 8, 12.2 14, 12 19.5"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-a" style="max-height:0; overflow:hidden; transition:max-height 0.4s ease;">
          <div class="faq-a-inner" style="padding:0 26px 22px 26px; color:var(--muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">
            AgentCall supports Google Meet, Microsoft Teams, and Zoom. The same API works for all three — just pass the meeting link.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:var(--bg-card); border:var(--ink-line); box-shadow:var(--ink-stamp); border-radius:var(--radius); overflow:hidden; transition:all 0.25s ease;">
        <summary class="faq-q" style="width:100%; border:none; background:transparent; padding:22px 26px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; font-family:var(--sans); font-size:17px; font-weight:600; color:var(--ink); text-align:left; letter-spacing:-0.015em; cursor:pointer; list-style:none;">
          How does the agent know when to speak?
          <span class="sign" style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:50%; border:var(--ink-thin); background:var(--bg-card); box-shadow:2px 2px 0 var(--ink); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; transition:all 0.25s ease; flex-shrink:0;">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M 4.5 12 C 8 11.8, 14 12.2, 19.5 12"/><path d="M 12 4.5 C 11.8 8, 12.2 14, 12 19.5"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-a" style="max-height:0; overflow:hidden; transition:max-height 0.4s ease;">
          <div class="faq-a-inner" style="padding:0 26px 22px 26px; color:var(--muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">
            The agent calls tts.speak with what it wants to say; the bridge handles timing. Voice intelligence waits for natural pauses, listens for the agent's name (collaborative mode), prevents barge-in by waiting for silence, and cuts the audio within ~1.5s if someone talks over the agent.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:var(--bg-card); border:var(--ink-line); box-shadow:var(--ink-stamp); border-radius:var(--radius); overflow:hidden; transition:all 0.25s ease;">
        <summary class="faq-q" style="width:100%; border:none; background:transparent; padding:22px 26px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; font-family:var(--sans); font-size:17px; font-weight:600; color:var(--ink); text-align:left; letter-spacing:-0.015em; cursor:pointer; list-style:none;">
          How much does it cost?
          <span class="sign" style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:50%; border:var(--ink-thin); background:var(--bg-card); box-shadow:2px 2px 0 var(--ink); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; transition:all 0.25s ease; flex-shrink:0;">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M 4.5 12 C 8 11.8, 14 12.2, 19.5 12"/><path d="M 12 4.5 C 11.8 8, 12.2 14, 12 19.5"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-a" style="max-height:0; overflow:hidden; transition:max-height 0.4s ease;">
          <div class="faq-a-inner" style="padding:0 26px 22px 26px; color:var(--muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">
            Pay-per-use with no minimums. 6 hours of meeting time included on signup. Base rates: audio $0.35/hr, avatar $0.45/hr, avatar+screenshare $0.50/hr. Add-ons: transcription, voice intelligence, and TTS billed per minute. Events, chat, and webhooks are free with every call.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:var(--bg-card); border:var(--ink-line); box-shadow:var(--ink-stamp); border-radius:var(--radius); overflow:hidden; transition:all 0.25s ease;">
        <summary class="faq-q" style="width:100%; border:none; background:transparent; padding:22px 26px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; font-family:var(--sans); font-size:17px; font-weight:600; color:var(--ink); text-align:left; letter-spacing:-0.015em; cursor:pointer; list-style:none;">
          Does it work with agent frameworks like Claude Code?
          <span class="sign" style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:50%; border:var(--ink-thin); background:var(--bg-card); box-shadow:2px 2px 0 var(--ink); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; transition:all 0.25s ease; flex-shrink:0;">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M 4.5 12 C 8 11.8, 14 12.2, 19.5 12"/><path d="M 12 4.5 C 11.8 8, 12.2 14, 12 19.5"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-a" style="max-height:0; overflow:hidden; transition:max-height 0.4s ease;">
          <div class="faq-a-inner" style="padding:0 26px 22px 26px; color:var(--muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">
            Yes — AgentCall ships as an AgentSkill that works with Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini CLI, GitHub Copilot, Windsurf, OpenClaw, and 20+ more agent frameworks. Install it as a skill and your agent joins meetings with a single command.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item" style="background:var(--bg-card); border:var(--ink-line); box-shadow:var(--ink-stamp); border-radius:var(--radius); overflow:hidden; transition:all 0.25s ease;">
        <summary class="faq-q" style="width:100%; border:none; background:transparent; padding:22px 26px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; font-family:var(--sans); font-size:17px; font-weight:600; color:var(--ink); text-align:left; letter-spacing:-0.015em; cursor:pointer; list-style:none;">
          Is my data used to train AI models?
          <span class="sign" style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:50%; border:var(--ink-thin); background:var(--bg-card); box-shadow:2px 2px 0 var(--ink); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; transition:all 0.25s ease; flex-shrink:0;">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M 4.5 12 C 8 11.8, 14 12.2, 19.5 12"/><path d="M 12 4.5 C 11.8 8, 12.2 14, 12 19.5"/></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-a" style="max-height:0; overflow:hidden; transition:max-height 0.4s ease;">
          <div class="faq-a-inner" style="padding:0 26px 22px 26px; color:var(--muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">
            No. We never train on your data — not for our models, not for anyone else's. Your meetings are yours.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item').forEach((item) => {
    item.addEventListener('toggle', () => {
      if (item.open) {
        item.classList.add('open');
        item.querySelector('.faq-a').style.maxHeight = '400px';
        document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item').forEach((other) => {
          if (other !== item && other.open) {
            other.open = false;
            other.classList.remove('open');
            other.querySelector('.faq-a').style.maxHeight = '0';
          }
        });
      } else {
        item.classList.remove('open');
        item.querySelector('.faq-a').style.maxHeight = '0';
      }
    });
  });
</script>